WEBVTT

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:07.160
Equip!

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:14.870
Galeon!

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:22.380
The G-Stone, embedded in Cyborg Gai's GaoBrace.

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:23.750
What is it?

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:29.000
2 years ago...

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:44.270
Gai!

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:47.170
So you survived, Gai!

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:48.970
Thank heavens!

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:57.410
The G-Stone, an infinite information circuit sealed by unknown technology.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:01.850
There was no way to keep Gai alive except by making a copy of...

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:04.360
...the drive system that powered the MechaLion.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:07.760
This is how the base energy source powering...

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:11.760
...both the cyborg and the vehicle robots was developed.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:15.100
And it is called the GS-Ride!

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:18.170
Ga-Ga-Ga, Ga-Ga-Ga, GaoGaiGar!

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:21.070
Ga-Ga-Ga, Ga-Ga-Ga-Ga, GaoGaiGar!!

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:28.140
King of Braves GaoGaiGar

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:32.070
Rise in fury, Steel Cyborg!

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:38.790
With your red mane and golden arms!

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:43.070
Your G-Stone sparkling in the sun...

00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:47.990
All the world's hope is in your hands.

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:51.910
Your time has come to make a stand!

00:01:51.910 --> 00:01:54.710
Crushing the hopes of the people...

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:58.470
The Zonders will pay the price!

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:03.470
Ga-Ga-Ga, Ga-Ga-Ga, GaoGaiGar!

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:06.640
Ga-Ga-Ga, Ga-Ga-Ga-Ga, GaoGaiGar!!

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:09.180
Final Fusion, approved!

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:12.310
Now transform into a superhero!

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:15.270
Warping dimensional space!

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:19.350
Dividing Driver!

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:26.990
A miracle! A mystery! The truth! A dream!

00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:32.870
A gigantic, invincible guardian is born!

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:35.820
Our very own King of Braves!

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:39.710
Ga-Ga-Ga-Ga, GaoGaiGar!!

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:41.920
This is the story of the brave men and women...

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:44.890
...who fight with all their hearts to save mankind.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:47.140
The Day the Sun Vanished

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:50.190
<i>The Day the Sun Vanished</i>

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:14.210
One day the sun suddenly vanished from the Kanto area.

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:18.340
There was no more warm spring sunshine in the city...

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:23.090
...and people were forced to rely on electricity for lighting, day and night.

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:36.980
A mammoth cloud, did you say?

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:42.490
According to our data, it's 99% identical to a cloud in composition.

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:45.410
In other words, a Zonder bent on destroying the environment, eh?

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:48.700
It's approximately 300 km in diameter, and it's expanding in all directions...

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:51.660
...at a speed of 40 meters per hour as we speak.

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:57.210
<i>74 hours have already passed since this cloud first appeared!</i>

00:03:57.420 --> 00:04:02.340
There's been a 300% surge in energy consumption in the Kanto area.

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:06.720
Most likely, the Zonder core is somewhere in the cloud's center...

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:08.680
...but the thing is... it's gigantic.

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:11.180
Are you sure it's a Zonder?

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:12.520
I'm positive it is!

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:17.230
We know you are, Mamoru.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:20.860
I promise you that we'll save your friends.

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:22.820
Uh-huh.

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:26.120
Ride with us, Mamoru!

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:28.280
Oh, come on, you guys!

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:31.450
You don't get a chance like this everyday!

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:34.620
Oh, um, that's okay, I'll be watching you from down here.

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:36.670
Really! You're such a coward!

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:41.170
Well, uh, I'm supposed to compete in an RC car race after this, so...

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:47.550
Um, I have a big English test later today, so I have to regretfully decline!

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:50.520
What about you two, Tezato and Suzuki?

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:55.390
What? Then that means we're the only ones going up...

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:58.860
You guys are all so spineless!

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:00.530
Oh, who cares?

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:03.900
If you don't want to ride with us, then we'll just go without you!

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:05.400
Well, you see...

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:10.790
Well! This is actually the 1 7th Annual Hot-air Balloon Festival.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:13.540
Have we really come that far?

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:17.460
It's such a pleasure, getting to see so many different balloons every year.

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:21.590
Really, the technology we have these days is so advanced.

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:26.550
Although there are a few balloons that are unmistakably duds.

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:30.760
Oh, it's such a smooth ride, not scary at all!

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:31.810
See?

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:34.890
Those dummies down there have no idea what they're missing!

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:41.690
Actually, I think the ice cream design might have something to do with it...

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:44.440
You think so too, then?

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:48.410
Takayasu's balloon looks like a poop, no matter how you look at it.

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:50.410
It's super-crappy, isn't it?

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:52.540
Sorry, Hana.

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:55.910
Maybe I should've gone along with you after all...

00:05:58.170 --> 00:05:58.670
Zonder!

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:03.420
What's going on?

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:04.800
Did something explode?

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:10.510
Hana!

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:15.220
Hana!

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:22.820
I couldn't protect Hana...

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:24.400
I couldn't!

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:25.780
Mamoru!

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:28.610
You've got your teammates at GGG on your side!

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:31.240
Let's go strike down that Zonder together!

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:32.330
Okay!

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:36.700
But we have insufficient data to formulate a strategy.

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:38.660
Then let us go!

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:43.250
As robots, we're not fazed by a little danger during intelligence-gathering!

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:46.630
EnRyu, this time the Zonder is attacking from the sky.

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:50.260
You and I have no way to become airborne except by the Mirror Catapult.

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:51.640
As such we're not suited for this task.

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:55.810
HyoRyu! You and I represent the pinnacle of cutting-edge technology.

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:58.890
What's the point if we aren't useful during an emergency like this?

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:02.980
That cloud is filled with highly-concentrated oxygen.

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:05.690
There's a good chance that...

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:08.820
...the heat from our drive systems could cause an explosion.

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:19.960
I'm taking StealthGao to infiltrate that cloud.

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:22.670
This is my job.

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:36.600
Are you all present, my Four Machine Kings?

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:57.870
All four of us are here, my lord.

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:02.580
Was it you who nurtured that behemoth Zonder, Pizza?

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:05.460
Indeed, it was my doing, Lord Pasdar.

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:11.800
That Zonder was a man I found wallowing in the filthy air of the city.

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:15.760
Man, those clouds have it made, what a carefree life.

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:20.060
What wouldn't I give to laze around all day without working...

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:23.060
The sky is indeed a marvelous thing...

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:24.600
Who the heck are you?

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:27.060
Forgive me, did I frighten you?

00:08:29.610 --> 00:08:31.400
I'll be happy to turn you into a cloud.

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:31.900
What?

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:34.950
Come now, take this.

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:55.760
And so the Zonder took to the skies...

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:59.470
As I have surrounded it with a plasma barrier...

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:02.680
...it will be impossible to infiltrate.

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:05.100
Well done, Pizza!

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:08.980
It won't be long now before our goals are achieved.

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:13.030
Now that he's surrounded by fresh air up in the sky...

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:16.110
...I'm sure he'll be quite pleased.

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:38.890
GaiGar, preparing to infiltrate the dark cloud.

00:09:45.890 --> 00:09:47.190
Gai, don't overdo it!

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:49.150
It looks like it's got a Zonder barrier made of plasma.

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:52.650
What, a barrier that's 300 km in diameter?

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:55.150
We were able to gather the data we needed.

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:57.570
Here's a magnified view of the cloud's structure.

00:09:59.410 --> 00:09:59.910
Huh?

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:03.540
So it built up static in the atmosphere...

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:07.670
...and sheathed itself in an energy barrier similar to lightning.

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:11.710
In other words, if we were to break through it...

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:14.000
...there'd be an explosion and Tokyo would disappear...

00:10:14.590 --> 00:10:15.800
Hold on a minute!

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:18.510
I've spotted airflow at the tip.

00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:20.180
Do you mean to say it's breathing?

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:22.010
It's like the mouth of a balloon, so to speak.

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:25.430
It seems to be inhaling air, and expelling nitrogen.

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:28.600
He's going to have to go through there to get inside!

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:31.730
That would only be possible if it wasn't so flammable...

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:33.070
Gai, did you get that?

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:35.030
I'm just going to have to give it a shot.

00:10:38.610 --> 00:10:40.950
GaiGar, on track to reach the tip of the Zonder in two minutes.

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:43.990
I'm picking up electromagnetic waves, as well as a tornado!

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:45.910
If these calculations are right...

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:49.420
...then it's got enough force to smash StealthGao's wings!

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:50.790
Gai, do you copy?

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:53.040
There's too much interference, we've lost contact!

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:21.070
Unable to locate GaiGar...

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:23.620
Is it possible that he crashed?

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:27.580
All those shockwaves could've easily smashed him to smithereens.

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:32.540
If even one of his electrical circuits was up, we'd be able to detect him...

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:36.670
Does that mean his cyborg life- support system's been knocked out?

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:40.300
No! The data's been cut off, that's all. I think...

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:43.550
Major...

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:45.760
No need to worry, Utsugi.

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:48.770
That idiot isn't going to go down so easily.

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:50.850
Big Brother Gai's alive.

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:53.560
Big Brother Gai's somewhere inside that cloud.

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:55.650
You can sense him, Mamoru?

00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:57.690
Yeah. It's just a feeling, really.

00:11:57.820 --> 00:11:59.280
But Big Brother Gai's alive!

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:04.700
Yes, past data shows that probability calculations don't apply to Captain Gai.

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:08.620
You're right. Gai will fulfill his mission and return safely.

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:12.120
That is what Gai must do to prove that he's a true hero!

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:20.970
Gai!

00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:23.720
Gai...

00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:24.800
Gai!

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:25.970
Gai!

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:27.720
Gai!

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:28.810
Gai!

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:32.730
Oh, it's you, Mikoto.

00:12:33.140 --> 00:12:34.810
Really, Gai, what are you thinking?

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:36.980
Taking a nap in a place like this?

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:41.900
Uh, it feels like I was asleep for a really long time.

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:46.120
Don't you have your pilot's test later on today?

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:48.160
Huh? Pilot?

00:12:49.030 --> 00:12:51.160
Oh, please. You're still half-asleep!

00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:53.830
You said you're going to the Space Development Center, remember?

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:57.580
Space Development Center?

00:12:58.880 --> 00:12:59.000
SPACE DEVELOPMENT CENTER

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:26.030
Equip!

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:34.870
Will Knife!

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:38.880
What have I...

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:40.420
Gai, you're going to be late.

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:42.130
You'd better get a move on!

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:46.260
Hey, listen to you! You sound just like my mom!

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:49.390
Oh! Sorry, I didn't mean to...

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:51.760
No, that's not what I meant.

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:53.720
I wasn't accusing you...

00:13:54.180 --> 00:13:56.730
I'm over what happened to my mom.

00:13:57.730 --> 00:14:01.150
So, uh, what was it I was supposed to do again?

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:04.030
Come on! Try to remember what it was on your own.

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:06.860
Remember what you've been doing until now...

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:11.910
What I've been doing until now?

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:16.830
Final Fusion!

00:14:30.300 --> 00:14:34.390
GaoGaiGar!

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:44.070
Broken Magnum!

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:46.490
Protect Shade!

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:11.090
Hey, thanks, Mikoto. I remember now.

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:13.350
I'm glad to hear that.

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:15.390
Okay, see you later.

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:17.720
Oh, wait a minute, Gai.

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:22.100
Take this with you.

00:15:22.230 --> 00:15:23.230
What is it?

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:26.400
It's a good luck charm, and you'd better not lose it!

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:31.990
Take it. So you'll never forget me.

00:15:32.320 --> 00:15:35.530
Are you crazy? I can't walk around with this, it's too embarrassing.

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:52.090
Thank you, Mikoto...

00:15:55.050 --> 00:15:58.810
The interior of the Zonder cloud... that's got to be the core!

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:01.480
Galeon!

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:12.240
The Projection Beam from Cyborg Gai's GaoBrace sends a unique...

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:17.530
...G-Stone signal to Galeon, enabling them to pinpoint each other's location.

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:18.830
Galeon!

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:23.370
Fusion!

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:36.850
GaiGar!

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:41.390
GaiGar, the result of a successful fusion between Gai and Galeon...

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:44.560
...when their respective G-Stones resonate.

00:17:15.430 --> 00:17:16.890
There they are!

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:31.900
Gai...

00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:32.610
Gai!

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:35.650
Big Brother Gai!

00:17:36.150 --> 00:17:39.570
Gai here. I've found everyone trapped inside the cloud.

00:17:39.950 --> 00:17:42.370
Luckily, the Zonder's so still it almost seems asleep.

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:45.410
Just do as I say and get the Mobile Unit ready!

00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:48.540
Ultra Technology Laboratory, launch!

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:53.920
Triple-decked Flying Carrier, Mirror Catapult, now opening!

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:58.340
Ul-Tech Engine, starting up!

00:17:58.590 --> 00:18:01.100
HyoRyu, Mirror Coating!

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:05.430
Launch!

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:09.230
The Ultra Technology Laboratory has arrived at its target!

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:12.440
EnRyu, Mirror Coating, launch!

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:22.200
Ultra Technology Laboratory, now on standby!

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:25.160
HyoRyu, EnRyu, now descending towards Ikebukuro.

00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:27.660
They'll be landing in less than a minute!

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:32.210
Now launching both GaoMachines!

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:39.720
Are you all right, EnRyu?

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:43.220
My A.I.'s no good at landing, see...

00:18:44.010 --> 00:18:45.390
There's no time to lose!

00:18:46.140 --> 00:18:49.100
The two GaoMachines are now infiltrating the Zonder Cloud.

00:18:49.600 --> 00:18:53.440
You'll make it for sure, won't you? Gai!

00:19:01.740 --> 00:19:05.120
Symmetrical Docking!

00:19:25.970 --> 00:19:28.140
The Dividing Driver is ready to go!

00:19:28.270 --> 00:19:30.060
Coordinates locked down!

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:34.150
Dividing Driver, launch!

00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:40.400
Dividing Driver, 8 minutes until docking!

00:19:43.280 --> 00:19:48.290
ChoRyuJin!

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:52.580
Eraser Head L, ready to go!

00:19:53.170 --> 00:19:55.670
Ready to activate Eraser Head L!

00:19:56.800 --> 00:19:59.510
Dividing Driver!

00:20:13.690 --> 00:20:14.770
Hana!

00:20:15.110 --> 00:20:17.070
A massive hot-air balloon Zonder...

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:22.070
Slit a hole at the top to expel all the hot air inside, and it'll shrivel up.

00:20:22.320 --> 00:20:26.200
Ingenious, Gai! You're a chip off the old block!

00:20:29.410 --> 00:20:33.250
Zonder contraction rate, 37.8%!

00:20:33.330 --> 00:20:36.210
Due to internal cooling, it's now descending.

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:38.210
It's on track to crash in less than 15 minutes!

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:40.380
Gai! Destroy that thing!

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:44.340
Hell and Heaven!

00:20:44.550 --> 00:20:47.760
Hell and Heaven!

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:27.470
You did it, ChoRyuJin!

00:21:27.840 --> 00:21:30.060
I'm glad to know you're safe, Captain.

00:21:46.910 --> 00:21:49.530
Gai, Welcome home.

00:21:51.240 --> 00:21:53.330
Curatio...

00:21:53.620 --> 00:21:56.870
...teneritas, sectio...

00:21:57.420 --> 00:22:01.170
...salus, coctura!

00:22:12.600 --> 00:22:14.600
Still, I wonder...

00:22:37.290 --> 00:22:40.580
What was it that I saw?

00:22:46.450 --> 00:22:50.350
You come floating down onto my planet.

00:22:51.550 --> 00:22:55.220
That's the dream I always have.

00:22:56.620 --> 00:23:01.400
Now you're looking up at the sky again...

00:23:01.400 --> 00:23:06.190
and you're searching for me.

00:23:06.820 --> 00:23:10.360
Longing to see you and be with you...

00:23:11.530 --> 00:23:17.290
I know I feel it just as strongly as you.

00:23:19.350 --> 00:23:24.050
When you and I are grown up...

00:23:24.050 --> 00:23:28.710
someday in the Sea of Stars.

00:23:29.400 --> 00:23:34.050
Give us the wings to fly

00:23:34.050 --> 00:23:40.950
and set off into the galaxy.
